### 4d. The keeper's idle cadence after the gate (M4F-1): part 4c's freeze with the keeper on its coverage
duties instead of a crank every second (Spec.keeper_rule, class Coverage).  'old keeper' = as built at M4R
(ECON §5.8): per second while ema_warm > 0, near a threshold (CR < 1.3 L) or |P_spot/P_ema - 1| > 2 %, and in
a duty-2 burst, which only a PRICE deviation starts; otherwise every 30 s.  A deposit-wrapped crank does not
move the price, so 29 of every 30 seconds after the gate are the attacker's: its buckets lift L_mlo, the
guard clears (+15 s), L_ema = L_mlo = the deposit's depth, and the reference blocks the genuine pump.  'M4F-1
keeper' (#98): per second also while ema_guard = 1, and a burst on a foreign bucket whose llo / lhi
deviates from the keeper's own sqrt(X*Y) by > 2 % (every LP-wrapped crank); its liquidity bursts are
REVERTED by #99 (a cheap keeper-cost DoS, M4G-2; keeper misses ratchet the freeze, M4G-1).  '#99 keeper' =
per second while ema_guard = 1, bursts on price only.  '#101 keeper' (FITS-2 (b)) = the #99 keeper plus
per-SECOND coverage for 10 s after a foreign bucket liquidity deviation on a market with positions, extended
while deviations recur (one crank per attacker second).  These carried positions exceed the candidate's
opening caps, so under #99 no window opens (part 11); the rows force the adoption.  'M4R' caps the EMA terms of
L_b at floor(D*1e4/lambda_min) (2D here); 'before M4F-1' has no cap.  RA -> cand SOL at lambda 99.78 %, flat W
s after the adoption, then a genuine pump to the top over 120 s; the attacker deposit-wraps one crank every
second from 'from' s (depK = K x the pool's LP counter deposited; from 40 = after an honest guard clear at
+9 s).  q is 5.9 % of the 314-SOL candidate's X, 2.9 % of the 630-SOL one's; the 320-SOL 4x row takes the
LiteSVM reproducer's candidate size and ramp (m4r_it::m4f1_*, where q is 3.1 % of X).  Cells: outcome;
attacker-only seconds after the gate; seconds the keeper observed.

