### 4e. Steady-state controls (no switch; M4F-1): a position at the size cap on a Raydium pool, the EMA
converged; the keeper on its coverage duties (Coverage, as in 4d; the guard is never set without a switch,
so the #99 keeper is the old keeper here and 'old keeper, M4R' is the rule after #99; '#101 keeper, M4R' is
the rule as adopted (#101): a deposit-wrapped crank deviates the bucket's lhi, so the keeper then covers every
second); the attacker deposit-wraps one crank every second (after the drain: from +60 s); flat W s, then a genuine
pump.  At the open caps (q/x <= 1.5 %) the push delays the liquidation by 0-2 s under the old keeper even
without the cap: the exposure of 4d is a switch's (a carried position that is large on the new pool).
Cells: outcome (seconds after the pump starts, price, lender P&L at the exit price, borrower remainder);
attacker-only seconds.

