## 5b. The steady-state withdraw drag under the keeper's real cadence (FITV-2, FITS-2; V2-14).  No switch: a
Tier C Raydium market whose unlocked LP the attacker holds (FITV-2's fork: a 160-SOL lambda 99.78 % 1 % CPMM
plus the attacker's own deposit of 1x / 3x / 3.95x the LP counter -> lambda 49.9 / 24.9 / 20.2 %), a position
at the open cap (in (iii) a share of it), the EMA converged.  The keeper follows its duties (every 30 s in
quiet periods; per second near a threshold or at |P_spot/P_ema - 1| > 2 %).  Every second, before the keeper,
the attacker sends [withdraw all, crank_price, deposit] -- an attacker-only second's bucket is the drained
depth D, so such seconds drag L_ema toward D (1/6 of the gap each), and the keeper's own observation in a
dragged second cannot lift it (the clamped observation is L_ema itself) -- and [withdraw all, liquidate,
deposit].  Flat for W s (the drag), then a genuine pump to the hold level over 60 s, held 300 s.  The rule sets:
'#100' = the spot leg at the drained L_live and the #99 keeper (29 of every 30 quiet seconds are the
attacker's, so L_ema reaches D within about 8 s); L_b = max(L_live, min(max(L_ema', L_slow), cap)), whose
L_slow term (V2-14) credits the depth that was there until it has followed the dragged L_ema (tau_slow = 1 h).
'#101' (as adopted, FITS-2) = the spot leg at max(L_live, L_ema') (a withdrawal in the same transaction
cannot make it true) and the #101 keeper, which covers every second for 10 s after a foreign bucket
liquidity deviation on a market with positions, extended while they recur: the attacker starts in the
second after a keeper observation, so its first dragged second is attacker-only (one step, L_ema x ~11/12);
every later second shares its bucket with the keeper's honest observation, which holds L_ema where it is.
'the withdrawn lows bound' = #100's first fix for FIT-2 (#100's exits), which bounded the EMA terms by
floor(L_mlo*1.01) = D (FITV-2).  Cells: outcome (seconds after the pump starts, by whom, price); for #101 the
keeper observations / attacker transactions over the run; L_ema / L_slow / L_mlo as a share of sqrt(X*Y)
at the pump.

