(iv) What is left under #101: the keeper's missed seconds (the M4G-1 class, downward), and pause-and-
resume drags.  While the attacker wraps every second, each second the keeper's observation does not land is
another attacker-only step (L_ema - D shrinks by 1/6), and a covered second's bucket holds L_ema, so the
steps add up; they need not be consecutive (no degraded mode).  An attacker that pauses until the coverage
window lapses (10 s) gets one attacker-only second per resumption, but the covered seconds of the pause
carry honest observations only and give back 1/6 of the gap each, so the drag does not accumulate.  The
