(v) The spot leg's own case (FITS-2 (a)): no drag, a genuine spike and retreat.  The price ramps to k x over
the ramp, holds, and falls back over 2 s to r x below the honest threshold: P_ema lags the spike, so for a
few seconds after the retreat the EMA leg is true while the robust spot at the pool's depth is not -- the
spot leg is the veto.  The unlocked-LP holder sends only [withdraw all, liquidate, deposit] every second,
before the keeper.  Under #100 the spot leg reads the drained L_live, the withdrawal makes it true, and the
liquidation of a position healthy at the pool's depth lands; under #101 it reads max(L_live, L_ema') and the
veto holds.  The #101 keeper alone (the spot leg at L_live) does not help: no attacker-only second is
involved.  Cells: the retreat levels r (of 1.98x, 2.00x, 2.01x, ..., 2.07x below the honest threshold) at
which the attacker's wrapped liquidation lands while the honest keeper leaves the position open.

