(vi) Liveness: a GENUINE withdrawal (FITS-2 (c)).  No attacker; every unlocked LP unit leaves the pool at
second 90 and stays out, so a position that is healthy at the pool's full depth becomes liquidatable at
its new depth.  Under #101 the spot leg reads max(L_live, L_ema'), and L_ema follows the drained depth at
1/6 of the gap per integrated second (tau = 5 s; the keeper observes every second near a threshold or
while |P_spot/P_ema - 1| > 2 %, else every 30 s, dt <= 2 s).  The EMA leg (the ring's reprojections at
L_ema) already waited for that decay under #100: in a flat or rising market it binds, and the new spot leg
costs nothing; it delays an exit only while the robust spot is below P_ema (a dip, noise), until L_ema has
decayed.  Positions where a band exists -- the drained buyback within delta of the reference, which L_b's
L_slow term keeps at the pre-withdrawal depth for about tau_slow: the 25-bps pool at the open cap and the
1 % pools at 0.3 of it.  Paths (x the starting price; h the middle of the band): 'flat h' = a 60-s ramp to
h, flat; 'dip d' = a 60-s ramp to h*(1 + d), flat, and the price back to h with the withdrawal (the
robust spot below P_ema); 'noise' = 'flat h' with +-1 % per-second noise (seeds 1-3); 'pump' = 1.2 h over
60 s, the withdrawal at second 30.  Cells: outcome, seconds after the withdrawal, price; the delay of #101
against #100.

