(vii) What is left under #101: a GENUINELY reached low, frozen (FITX-1, the verification of #101).  The
attacker withdraws its unlocked LP for real at second 1 and keeps it out for `held` s, cranking every second
at the drained depth -- the keeper reads the same depth, so nothing is foreign and no coverage starts, and
L_ema genuinely falls toward D (at lambda 49.9 %: 0.741 / 0.667 / 0.566 / 0.510 of the full depth after
3 / 5 / 10 / 20 s).  It then re-deposits and withdraw-wraps a crank every second: its first wrap starts the
keeper's per-second coverage, and every later bucket holds the drained and the keeper's honest observation,
[D, H], which leaves L_ema where it is (the clamped observation is L_ema itself) -- the freeze, at one keeper
crank per attacker transaction.  L_slow follows the drained lows (its input is min(lobs, L_mlo), and every
bucket's low is D; tau_slow = 1 h), as after a withdrawal for good.
After W s flat, the genuine pump to the hold level, with [withdraw all, liquidate, deposit] every second: the
spot leg reads max(L_live, L_ema') = the frozen low, the EMA leg the same low, and where delta covers the
drained cost (or L_slow has followed) the exit bound passes.  Cells: forced hold levels (from 1.80x, below the
honest threshold with the LP in the pool).  'The LP out for good': the same LP withdraws at second 1 and
stays out, nobody else acts -- the genuine withdrawal the protocol liquidates on (FITS-2 (c)); for every
forced level of the row, whether the honest keeper liquidates it then too, no later (count, and the smallest
lag of the forced liquidation behind it, in seconds).

