## 11. Switch only if all fit (#99, owner decision 2026-09-29; ECON §6.1, §6.2, §12.12 (11); ARCH §2.6
rule 3).  A proposal that opens or improves a window whose adoption carries open positions, and the
execution, also need every open position to fit the candidate's normal opening caps as an open on it right
after the adoption: X0 = min(X_cand, min(L_slow, D)/sqrt(p), D/(lambda_min*sqrt(p))) <= D/sqrt(p), the
candidate's locked token reserve (the execution without X_cand), at p = min(P_ema, P_cand) and at P_ema;
min(max_q_hwm, sum Q) <= min(impact cap, 3.00*phi*X0) and sum Q <= min(OI cap, 7.50*phi*X0), phi =
min(phi_inc, phi_cand) since FIT-2's fix (#100; phi_inc = Market.min_open_fee_ppm, the lowest fee an open paid
since the market last had no position) and at most 2,500 ppm since FITS-1 (#101; CARRIED_FEE_CAP_PPM)
(Market.carried_fit; CarriedPositionsTooLarge / cancelled).  Parts 1-10 force the adoption to study its
mechanics; this part applies the rule.

