### 11d. FIT-2: a carried position on a higher-fee candidate, and fast pumps (engine P, fit enforced, the #101
keeper).  On a 1 % pool the per-position impact cap binds (2.47 % of X0) where 25 bps' fee-scaled cap is
0.75 %, and a carried position's margin was posted on the incumbent's cost: V/B on the new pool is lower than
for a position of the same size opened there.  RAC = RA's 2,500-SOL lambda 50 % 0.25 % AMM v4 pool at Tier C
(the fork's M4X-2 / FIT-2 market), RA the same pool at Tier A, RAC1 the same pool at a 1 % fee; the candidate
a lambda 99.78 % pool at a 1 % fee; flat W s after the adoption, then a genuine pump to 4x over R s.  '#99's
fit at phi_cand' is the rule FIT-2 broke (the carried fee-scaled caps at the candidate's fee); '#100's fit' the
carried fee-scaled caps at min(phi_inc, phi_cand) (phi_inc = Market.min_open_fee_ppm, the lowest fee an open
paid since the market last had no position), which FITS-1 broke at a 1 % -> 1 % switch; 'M4R' is the rule as
adopted (#101): the carried fee-scaled caps at min(phi_inc, phi_cand, 2,500 ppm), the impact caps unchanged,
the exit reference of #99, the spot leg at max(L_live, L_ema').  Both analysis fits run with the exits and the
keeper as adopted.  Cells: outcome (time after the adoption, price vs pre-halt; delay against the control of
the same W and ramp), lender P&L at the exit price.

(i) FIT-2's positions: RAC -> 320 SOL at 1 %, the position at 100 % / 76 % of #99's fit limit, under #99's fit
at phi_cand (the adoption allowed) and under M4R (#101).

