### 11e. FIT-3: a closed large position keeps the mark (residual 14; max_q_hwm resets only when
open_positions reaches 0).  RA's market (Tier A, 30-day terms): three honest positions of 0.25 x the
incumbent's size cap, opened on days 0 / 10 / 20; with the griefer, one borrower opens at the incumbent's
cap on day 20 and closes a second later.  The incumbent halts on day 21; the only candidate has 40 % of its
reserves at lambda 99.78 %, and every honest position and their OI fit it.  The fit bounds every open q by
min(max_q_hwm, sum Q): the griefer's closed position keeps the first term at the cap, so the candidate is
refused until the S3 exits bring sum Q down to its per-position cap.  Each healthy position on the halted
pool is frozen at the pre-halt P_ema and settles S3 at its own deadline (fair value, the expiry fee as p');
one carried by the adoption expires on the new pool.  Cells: time after the halt; sum Q / the incumbent's
cap after the event; the lender's P&L against holding q (at the frozen P_ema for S3, else the exit price).

